IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`

-- aia-timeline: the time axis of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, "the Omnibus").
-- Articles 111 and 113 as enacted and as amended, and the Omnibus's Article 4 (its entry into force).
-- READ-ONLY for the parts. A part calls exactly these (PLAN.md section 7 has the signatures):
--   `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force`                    the version function
--   `Art 113 the provision group applies`                   the applicability function (Art 113 with Art 111(2)'s saving)
--   `Art 111(1) ...`, `Art 111(2) ...`, `Art 111(3) ...`, `Art 111(4) ...`   the stand-alone transitional rules
-- Every other name in this file is a helper that the tests exercise; a part never calls one.
-- The Publications Office consolidation (line numbers "src:N") is a documentation tool with no
-- legal effect; the as-enacted wording is quoted from the base file (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:N).
-- A result of NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTHING-kind); a result of FALSE from a gate means
-- only that the group does not apply on that date, and the caller turns it into NOTHING.

§ `Entry into force of the Regulation and of the Omnibus`

-- src:4 | | | REGULATION (EU) 2024/1689 OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL of 13 June 2024 laying down harmonised rules on artificial intelligence and amending Regulations (EC) No 300/2008, (EU) No 167/2013, (EU) No 168/2013, (EU) 2018/858, (EU) 2018/1139 and (EU) 2019/2144 and Directives 2014/90/EU, (EU) 2016/797 and (EU) 2020/1828 (Artificial Intelligence Act) (Text with EEA relevance) (OJ L 1689 12.7.2024, p. 1) |
@ref Art 113 first paragraph: the date of publication is in the title block (src:4)
`Art 113 the Regulation was published` MEANS Date 12 7 2024

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
@ref Art 113 first paragraph (src:1656)
`Art 113 the Regulation enters into force` MEANS `Art 113 the Regulation was published` PLUS 20  -- "the twentieth day following": 12 July plus 20 days is 1 August 2024

-- src:9 | | | REGULATION (EU) 2026/1744 OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL of 8 July 2026 | L 1744 | 1 | 24.7.2026 |
@ref Omnibus Art 4: the date of publication is in the list of amending acts (src:9)
`Omnibus Art 4 the Omnibus was published` MEANS Date 24 7 2026

-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:764 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the third day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
@ref Omnibus Art 4 first paragraph (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:764)
`Omnibus Art 4 the Omnibus enters into force` MEANS `Omnibus Art 4 the Omnibus was published` PLUS 3  -- "the third day following": 24 July plus 3 days is 27 July 2026

-- The version function. The Omnibus amends the text on the day it enters into force; before that
-- the text as enacted is the text (the as-enacted Regulation is the only text there ever was before 27 July 2026).
@ref Omnibus Art 4 first paragraph: the amendments of its Article 1 take effect on its entry into force
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Version of the Regulation`
`Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `Omnibus Art 4 the Omnibus enters into force`
    THEN `as amended`
    ELSE `as enacted`

@ref Art 113 first paragraph: the Regulation exists from its entry into force
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 113 the Regulation is in force` MEANS
    `the date asked` AT LEAST `Art 113 the Regulation enters into force`

