-- src:1666 | (ii) 2 August 2028 as regards AI systems classified as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(1) and Annex I;
@ref Art 113 third paragraph point (c) (src:1664-1666)
`Art 113(c)(i) Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to Annex III systems from` MEANS Date 2 12 2027

@ref Art 113 third paragraph point (c)(ii)
`Art 113(c)(ii) Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to Annex I systems from` MEANS Date 2 8 2028

-- src:1668 | (d) Articles 102 to 110 shall apply from 27 July 2026.
@ref Art 113 third paragraph point (d) (src:1668)
`Art 113(d) Articles 102 to 110 apply from` MEANS Date 27 7 2026

-- The three dates that only the text as enacted gives.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2199 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202 | Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025;
@ref Art 113 as enacted: second paragraph and point (a) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2199-2202)
`Art 113 as enacted the general date of application` MEANS Date 2 8 2026

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2206 | Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations in this Regulation shall apply from 2 August 2027.
@ref Art 113 as enacted point (c): Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2206)
`Art 113(c) as enacted Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations apply from` MEANS Date 2 8 2027

§ `Article 113 as enacted: when each provision group applies`

-- The date from which a provision group applies in the text as enacted.
-- Point (c) as enacted names "Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations" only: the encoding reads
-- "the corresponding obligations" as Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 for a system that is high-risk through Article 6(1).
-- The Article 5 additions did not exist as enacted. A system that is not high-risk has no date in Chapter III Sections 1 to 3.
@ref Art 113 as enacted
GIVEN `the provision group` IS A `Provision group`
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 113 as enacted the date of application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision group`
    WHEN `Chapter I` THEN JUST `Art 113(a) Chapters I and II apply from`
    WHEN `Chapter II` THEN JUST `Art 113(a) Chapters I and II apply from`
    WHEN `Article 5 additions` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Article 5(1)(ba), (bb), (1a), (1b) are not in the text as enacted
    WHEN `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` THEN JUST `Art 113(b) the group of Chapter III Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Article 78 applies from`
    WHEN `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` THEN
        CONSIDER `the route to high-risk`
        WHEN `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` THEN JUST `Art 113(c) as enacted Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations apply from`
        WHEN `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` THEN JUST `Art 113 as enacted the general date of application`
        WHEN `Route neither` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 give no date to a system that is not high-risk
    WHEN `Articles 102 to 110` THEN JUST `Art 113 as enacted the general date of application`
    WHEN General THEN JUST `Art 113 as enacted the general date of application`

§ `Article 113 as amended: when each provision group applies`

-- The date from which a provision group applies in the text as amended.
-- Articles 6(5) and 101 are in the group General: point (b) excepts Article 101 and point (c) excepts Article 6(5), so the second paragraph reaches them.
@ref Art 113 as amended
GIVEN `the provision group` IS A `Provision group`
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 113 as amended the date of application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision group`
    WHEN `Chapter I` THEN JUST `Art 113(a) Chapters I and II apply from`
    WHEN `Chapter II` THEN JUST `Art 113(a) Chapters I and II apply from`
    WHEN `Article 5 additions` THEN JUST `Art 113(a) the Article 5 additions apply from`
    WHEN `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` THEN JUST `Art 113(b) the group of Chapter III Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Article 78 applies from`
    WHEN `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` THEN
        CONSIDER `the route to high-risk`
        WHEN `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` THEN JUST `Art 113(c)(ii) Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to Annex I systems from`
        WHEN `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` THEN JUST `Art 113(c)(i) Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to Annex III systems from`
        WHEN `Route neither` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): point (c) gives a date only "as regards AI systems classified as high-risk"
    WHEN `Articles 102 to 110` THEN JUST `Art 113(d) Articles 102 to 110 apply from`
    WHEN General THEN JUST `Art 113 second paragraph the general date of application`

§ `Article 111(2): the saving for high-risk AI systems already on the market`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2159 | 2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2026, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs. In any case, the providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations of this Regulation by 2 August 2030.
@ref Art 111(2) as enacted: "before 2 August 2026" (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2159)
`Art 111(2) as enacted the date before which a placed system is saved` MEANS Date 2 8 2026

-- "Without prejudice to the application of Article 5": the groups of Chapter II and the Article 5 additions are never saved.
-- Chapter I is not named in the saving, so it is saved like the rest (a question about Chapter I that is not about one
-- high-risk system passes `Route neither`, and then nothing is saved).
@ref Art 111(2) first sentence, both versions: "Without prejudice to the application of Article 5"
GIVEN `the provision group` IS A `Provision group`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 111(2) the provision group can be saved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision group`
    WHEN `Chapter II` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Article 5 additions` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Text as enacted: a high-risk AI system placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2026
-- is outside the Regulation unless, from that date, it is subject to significant changes in its design.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2159 | 2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2026, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs. In any case, the providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations of this Regulation by 2 August 2030.
@ref Art 111(2) as enacted first sentence (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2159)
GIVEN `the provision group` IS A `Provision group`
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 111(2) as enacted the system is saved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route to high-risk`
    WHEN `Route neither` THEN FALSE  -- not a high-risk AI system: the saving speaks of operators of high-risk AI systems only
    OTHERWISE
            `Art 111(2) the provision group can be saved` `the provision group`
        AND `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` LESS THAN `Art 111(2) as enacted the date before which a placed system is saved`
        AND (NOT `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

-- Text as amended: the date is "the date of application of Chapter III referred to in Article 113", which is
-- one date for a system classified under Annex III and another for a system classified under Annex I (see the fork register).
-- src:1623 | 2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113, third paragraph, point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before the date of application of Chapter III referred to in Article 113, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs. In any case, the providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2030.
@ref Art 111(2) as amended first sentence (src:1623)
GIVEN `the provision group` IS A `Provision group`
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 111(2) as amended the system is saved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 113 as amended the date of application` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the route to high-risk`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE  -- not a high-risk AI system: the saving speaks of operators of high-risk AI systems only
    WHEN JUST `the date of application of Chapter III` THEN
            `Art 111(2) the provision group can be saved` `the provision group`
        AND `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` LESS THAN `the date of application of Chapter III`
        AND (NOT `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

§ `Article 113 with Article 111(2): the applicability function`

-- Has the date of application come?
GIVEN `the date of application` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 113 the date of application has come` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date of application`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE  -- no date of application exists in the case
    WHEN JUST `the date` THEN `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date`

-- The text as enacted.
@ref Art 113 and Art 111(2) as enacted
GIVEN `the provision group` IS A `Provision group`
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 113 as enacted the provision group applies` MEANS
        `Art 113 the Regulation is in force` `the date asked`
    AND `Art 113 the date of application has come` (`Art 113 as enacted the date of application` `the provision group` `the route to high-risk`) `the date asked`
    AND (NOT `Art 111(2) as enacted the system is saved` `the provision group` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

-- The text as amended.
@ref Art 113 and Art 111(2) as amended
GIVEN `the provision group` IS A `Provision group`
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 113 as amended the provision group applies` MEANS
        `Art 113 the Regulation is in force` `the date asked`
    AND `Art 113 the date of application has come` (`Art 113 as amended the date of application` `the provision group` `the route to high-risk`) `the date asked`
    AND (NOT `Art 111(2) as amended the system is saved` `the provision group` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

-- THE APPLICABILITY FUNCTION. Does the provision group apply on the date asked, to an AI system of this route, placed
-- on the date given, and significantly changed in its design or not since? It dispatches on the version in force on the date asked.
-- A question that is not about one AI system passes `Route neither` and any date (the core's constant is made for it).
-- A system that is a component of a large-scale IT system under Annex X is not a case of Art 111(2): ask Art 111(1) too.
-- FALSE means "does not apply on the date asked"; the caller's layer-1 function then answers NOTHING, never JUST FALSE.
@ref Art 113 and Art 111(2), both versions
GIVEN `the provision group` IS A `Provision group`
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 113 the provision group applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
    WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                                                 -- VERSION as enacted
        `Art 113 as enacted the provision group applies` `the provision group` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
    WHEN `as amended` THEN                                                                 -- VERSION as amended
        `Art 113 as amended the provision group applies` `the provision group` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

§ `Article 111(1): large-scale IT systems (Annex X)`

-- src:1620 | 1. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), AI systems which are components of the large-scale IT systems established by the legal acts listed in Annex X that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2027 shall be brought into compliance with this Regulation by 31 December 2030.
@ref Art 111(1) first subparagraph, unchanged by the Omnibus (src:1620)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system established by a legal act listed in Annex X` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 111(1) the date by which the AI system must be brought into compliance` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 113 the Regulation is in force` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Regulation did not exist before its entry into force
    ELSE IF       `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system established by a legal act listed in Annex X`
              AND `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` LESS THAN Date 2 8 2027
         THEN JUST (Date 31 12 2030)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule reaches components placed or put into service before 2 August 2027

-- Article 111(1), second subparagraph: what the requirements of this Regulation mean for the evaluation of those systems.
-- It addresses whoever undertakes the evaluation; it gives a provider or deployer nothing to do (see NOTES.md, Jural relations).
-- src:1621 | The requirements laid down in this Regulation shall be taken into account in the evaluation of each large-scale IT system established by the legal acts listed in Annex X to be undertaken as provided for in those legal acts and where those legal acts are replaced or amended.
@ref Art 111(1) second subparagraph (src:1621)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the evaluation of the large-scale IT system is being undertaken as provided for in the legal acts listed in Annex X` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal acts listed in Annex X are being replaced or amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 111(1) the requirements of this Regulation are to be taken into account in the evaluation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 113 the Regulation is in force` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Regulation did not exist before its entry into force
    ELSE IF       `the evaluation of the large-scale IT system is being undertaken as provided for in the legal acts listed in Annex X`
               OR `the legal acts listed in Annex X are being replaced or amended`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names the evaluation and the replacement or amendment of the acts

§ `Article 111(2), second sentence: high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2159 | 2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2026, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs. In any case, the providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations of this Regulation by 2 August 2030.
@ref Art 111(2) as enacted second sentence (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2159)
GIVEN `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 111(2) as enacted the date by which providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities must comply` MEANS
    IF `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities`
    THEN JUST (Date 2 8 2030)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities

-- src:1623 | 2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113, third paragraph, point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before the date of application of Chapter III referred to in Article 113, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs. In any case, the providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2030.
@ref Art 111(2) as amended second sentence (src:1623)
GIVEN `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 111(2) as amended the date by which providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities must comply` MEANS
    IF `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities`
    THEN JUST (Date 2 8 2030)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities

-- The wording changed ("of this Regulation" became "laid down in this Regulation"); the date and the addressees did not.
@ref Art 111(2) second sentence, both versions
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 111(2) the date by which providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities must comply` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 113 the Regulation is in force` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Regulation did not exist before its entry into force
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 111(2) as enacted the date by which providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities must comply` `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities`   -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 111(2) as amended the date by which providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities must comply` `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities`   -- VERSION as amended

§ `Article 111(3): general-purpose AI models already on the market`

-- src:1625 | 3. Providers of general-purpose AI models that have been placed on the market before 2 August 2025 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2027.
@ref Art 111(3), unchanged by the Omnibus (src:1625)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the general-purpose AI model was placed on the market` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 111(3) the date by which the provider of a general-purpose AI model already on the market must comply` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 113 the Regulation is in force` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Regulation did not exist before its entry into force
    ELSE IF `the date the general-purpose AI model was placed on the market` LESS THAN Date 2 8 2025
         THEN JUST (Date 2 8 2027)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule reaches models placed on the market before 2 August 2025

§ `Article 111(4): AI systems generating synthetic content (inserted by the Omnibus)`

-- src:1627 | 4. Providers of AI systems, including general-purpose AI systems, generating synthetic audio, image, video or text content, that have been placed on the market before 2 August 2026 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply with Article 50(2) by 2 December 2026.
@ref Art 111(4), inserted by the Omnibus (src:1627)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market` IS A DATE
      `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 111(4) the date by which the provider of an AI system generating synthetic content must comply with Article 50(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
    WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 4 is not in the text as enacted
    WHEN `as amended` THEN          -- VERSION as amended
        IF       `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content`
             AND `the date the AI system was placed on the market` LESS THAN Date 2 8 2026
        THEN JUST (Date 2 12 2026)
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule reaches systems placed on the market before 2 August 2026

§ `The regulative rules of Article 111 (the breach path of each deadline)`

-- The party of each rule is a Role of the core. The clock of a trace is the day number (`Day date`), so a trace event
-- is stamped with the date it happens on: `AT (Day (Date 31 12 2030))`. A rule that does not arise on the date asked
-- is FULFILLED: nothing is owed (the decision function above answers NOTHING; trace the rule only where it arises).
DECLARE `Art 111 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 111(1) bring the AI system into compliance with this Regulation`
    `Art 111(2) take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations`
    `Art 111(3) take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation`
    `Art 111(4) take the necessary steps to comply with Article 50(2)`

-- Article 111(1): "shall be brought into compliance". The text names no party. The encoding takes the operator (Art 3(8)); see the fork register.
@ref Art 111(1) first subparagraph
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system established by a legal act listed in Annex X` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 111 act`
`Art 111(1) the duty to bring the AI system into compliance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 111(1) the date by which the AI system must be brought into compliance` `the date asked` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system established by a legal act listed in Annex X`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts
    WHEN JUST `the deadline` THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 111(1) bring the AI system into compliance with this Regulation`
        WITHIN (Day `the deadline`) MINUS (Day `Art 113 the Regulation enters into force`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the AI system was not brought into compliance with this Regulation by the date Article 111(1) gives"

-- Article 111(2), second sentence: the provider. The Deployer's duty is the next rule; the two are one relation each (one party, one act).
@ref Art 111(2) second sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 111 act`
`Art 111(2) the provider's duty to take the necessary steps` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 111(2) the date by which providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities must comply` `the date asked` `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts
    WHEN JUST `the deadline` THEN
        PARTY Provider
        MUST `Art 111(2) take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations`
        WITHIN (Day `the deadline`) MINUS (Day `Art 113 the Regulation enters into force`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the necessary steps were not taken by the date Article 111(2) gives"

@ref Art 111(2) second sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 111 act`
`Art 111(2) the deployer's duty to take the necessary steps` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 111(2) the date by which providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities must comply` `the date asked` `the AI system is a high-risk AI system intended to be used by public authorities`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts
    WHEN JUST `the deadline` THEN
        PARTY Deployer
        MUST `Art 111(2) take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations`
        WITHIN (Day `the deadline`) MINUS (Day `Art 113 the Regulation enters into force`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the necessary steps were not taken by the date Article 111(2) gives"

@ref Art 111(3)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the general-purpose AI model was placed on the market` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 111 act`
`Art 111(3) the duty of the provider of a general-purpose AI model already on the market` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 111(3) the date by which the provider of a general-purpose AI model already on the market must comply` `the date asked` `the date the general-purpose AI model was placed on the market`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts
    WHEN JUST `the deadline` THEN
        PARTY Provider
        MUST `Art 111(3) take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation`
        WITHIN (Day `the deadline`) MINUS (Day `Art 113 the Regulation enters into force`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the necessary steps were not taken by the date Article 111(3) gives"

@ref Art 111(4)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market` IS A DATE
      `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 111 act`
`Art 111(4) the duty of the provider of an AI system generating synthetic content` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 111(4) the date by which the provider of an AI system generating synthetic content must comply with Article 50(2)` `the date asked` `the date the AI system was placed on the market` `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts
    WHEN JUST `the deadline` THEN
        PARTY Provider
        MUST `Art 111(4) take the necessary steps to comply with Article 50(2)`
        WITHIN (Day `the deadline`) MINUS (Day `Omnibus Art 4 the Omnibus enters into force`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the necessary steps to comply with Article 50(2) were not taken by the date Article 111(4) gives"
